    "result_text": "The remaining `CheckDigits` references are the correct usage (the class name and the Luhn call that computes the CHK segment). Everything is coherent.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`, formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties; added `memberId` (documenting the `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` format). This regenerates `OwnerDto` accordingly.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Renamed the stored field `customerCode` (`customer_code`) \u2192 `memberId` (`member_id`), with matching getter/setter.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` now auto-maps from the stored field.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced `assignCustomerCode` with `assignMemberId`, which builds `<REGION>` + 2-digit fiscal year + the 8-hex SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) HASH8 + a Luhn CHK over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`, with collision de-duplication now applied to the `memberId`. The audit line, the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event, and the owner segment all reference the `memberId`.\n\n6. **`CheckDigits.java`** \u2014 Updated the doc comment; the Luhn helper still computes the CHK segment.\n\n**Test results:** 68 tests run, **66 pass** \u2014 including all 11 tests targeting this change (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp21, Cp31, Cp32, Cp41, Cp43, Cp48, Cp53, Cp56).\n\nThe 2 remaining failures (`Cp23`, `Cp39`) are **pre-existing and unrelated** to this task \u2014 they concern household membership-level *capping* (`expected:<3> but was:<2>`), a code path I did not modify. I verified this by reverting my changes and re-running those two tests: they fail identically on the original code, so they were never green. Fixing them would require changing unrelated membership-capping behaviour outside the scope of this memberId-unification task.",
